# Security assessment HAR captures contain live tokens/cookies — never commit.
security-check/*.har

# Captured request payloads contain live seller data (boutique ids, prices,
# purchase-price margins, barcodes) and would carry auth headers if re-captured
# with them — never commit. Keep captures in a scratchpad outside the repo.
*-payload.txt
SECURITY-register-guest.md

# Local gate-notification config — holds the Telegram bot token (secret).
# Keep it local; never commit the secret. Copy .claude/notifications.example.json
# to .claude/notifications.json and fill in botToken, or supply WF_TELEGRAM_* env.
.claude/notifications.json

# Backend body-contract working docs. These describe the shop-product create/update
# request contract by reading BACKEND SOURCE, and record unpatched backend defects
# (boutique ownership not checked, client-controllable `id` on create, no barcode
# uniqueness on update, approval-queue bypass) with exact backend file:line
# citations. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC — committing them would publish a working
# exploitation guide for a live system. Keep them local; share via the backend
# team's own channel, never via this repo.
docs/api-requirements/shop-product-body-contract.md
docs/api-requirements/shop-product-body-payloads.txt
docs/api-requirements/seller-product-body-alignment-roadmap.md
Guest-Authentication-&-Token-Renewal.md
go-refresh-api-contract.md
# Same class: the core backend's auth contract (endpoint shapes, token TTLs and
# server-side config names) plus the implementation plan that quotes it. Keep
# local; share through the backend team's own channel, never via this repo.
laravel-refresh-flow.md
laravel-refresh-plan.md

# Same class: the shop-locations backend contract (endpoint shapes, permission
# names and the seller-scoping rules). Keep local; share through the backend
# team's own channel, never via this repo.
seller-dashboard-locations-api-contract.md
docs/testing/TESTING_STACK_AND_ROADMAP.md
